<div class="content-panel-body">
<p>I keep a quote pinned above my desk. F. Scott Fitzgerald wrote it almost a century ago, and I've been thinking about it a lot this month. "The test of a first-rate intelligence," he wrote, "is the ability to hold two opposed ideas in mind at the same time, and still retain the ability to function." That, more than anything else, is what good investing looks like right now.</p>
