<p>I want to leave you with one more thought. As Australians grapple with fuel shortages and rising costs, the response from Canberra has been to encourage people to exercise "common sense." Ronald Reagan, forty years ago, had a line for moments like this. He said the nine most terrifying words in the English language are: "I'm from the government and I'm here to help." Some things don't change.</p>
